 "about_text": "18th Street Arts Center is a nonprofit artist residency and public-programs organization in Santa Monica, California, founded in 1988 by Susanna Bixby Dakin and Linda Frye Burnham out of a 1970s-80s community of feminist and performance artists that included Judy Chicago and Barbara T. Smith. Now one of the largest artist-residency programs in Southern California, it hosts local, national, and international artists for live/work studio stays, alongside organizations-in-residence such as Highways Performance Space. Its program blends exhibitions and public events in the Atrium Gallery and Artist's Hearth with community-engagement initiatives like Culture Mapping 90404, reflecting a long-standing commitment to socially engaged, research-driven contemporary art practice.",
